----- stdout -----
Open-source database audit trail engine and CLI

Usage: auditstream [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init     Generate audit schema and trigger migrations
  status   Show audit schema, trigger and partition status
  verify   Verify triggers, schema integrity and default partition health
  history  Inspect recorded audit history and diffs
  export   Export recorded audit events to a sink
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --config <PATH>
          Path to the configuration file (defaults to ./auditstream.toml if present)
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_CONFIG=]

      --database-url <URL>
          Postgres connection URL (also reads `DATABASE_URL` as fallback)
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_DATABASE_URL]

      --schema <SCHEMA>
          Audit schema name (defaults to `auditstream`)
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_SCHEMA=]

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (`-v` info, `-vv` debug)

  -q, --quiet
          Silence warnings and info logs (errors only)

      --log-format <LOG_FORMAT>
          Format for stderr log messages

          Possible values:
          - text: Human-readable plain text logs (default)
          - json: Structured single-line JSON log records on stderr
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_LOG_FORMAT=]
          [default: text]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

----- stderr -----
